        "title": "isa_realize() may not exist in the ISA API; possible build break",
        "explanation": "The container realizes its embedded children with isa_realize(). As far as I recall, the ISA bus API only provides isa_realize_and_unref(), and this diff touches only i8259.c, so nothing here adds isa_realize(). If no other change adds it, the file will not compile. Do not switch to isa_realize_and_unref(): it would drop a reference that object_initialize_child() makes the parent own.",
        "suggestion": "Use qdev_realize(pri_dev, BUS(s->isabus), errp) and qdev_realize(sec_dev, BUS(s->isabus), errp), or make sure isa_realize() is added in the same series.",
